 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Canberra is in the Australian Capital Territory (ACT). Its unemployment rate in September 2026, the latest month available, was:\n\n- **Trend: 4.2%.** This is the better guide to the underlying rate. It has stayed in a narrow 4.1–4.2% band since late 2025, and it was 4.17% in August 2026.\n- **Original (not seasonally adjusted): 4.7%.** This was up from 3.9% in August 2026.\n\nThe ABS doesn't publish a seasonally adjusted series for the ACT in this dataset. That's the measure news reports usually quote for the national rate. The original figures also swing a lot from month to month. They ranged from 3.3% in December 2025 to 4.8% in April 2026, so the September jump is probably mostly noise.",
